// sent as `X-Webhook-Signature: sha256=<hex>` plus `X-Webhook-Timestamp`. Opsflow rejects
// timestamps older than 5 minutes. The signature covers the exact bytes the HTTP node sends,
// which is why that node sends this `body` string as a raw body.
// (Code node mode: Run Once for All Items.)
// HMAC-SHA256 as lowercase hex, matching Opsflow's lib/webhooks.ts signPayload. Uses Node's
// crypto when this n8n instance allows require('crypto'); otherwise falls back to the small
// pure-JS implementation below (no imports needed).
